/*
 * Declares the MapIteratorDelValue class.
 *
 * MapIteratorDelValue represents the destruction of a map iterator. Ymir map
 * iterators are dynamically allocated so they remain valid even when the map is
 * structurally modified during iteration. Once iteration is complete, the
 * iterator must be explicitly destroyed to release its internal resources.
 *
 * This operator is typically emitted in a `finally` scope associated with a
 * map iteration construct.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::map::iteration::del
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/map/iteration/del.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2024-11-15
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
